    <!-- Guide Screen -->
    <string name="guide_title">HDR MASTERING GUIDE</string>
    <string name="faq_q1">Is SDR to HDR true HDR?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">SDR to HDR uses inverse tone mapping on the GPU. It expands highlights toward 1000 nits and maps Rec.709 primaries into BT.2020. While it makes OLED screens glow vividly, it cannot restore clipped camera sensor data that was never captured.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">Why do uploads look different on Instagram/TikTok?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">Social media platforms often compress or tone-map uploaded video into standard SDR if their ingestion pipeline does not support HDR10. YouTube supports full HDR10 playback natively.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">Does conversion use battery or generate heat?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">Processing 4K60 video heavily taxes the hardware encoder and GPU. Hivid monitors thermal throttling and uses efficient EGL hardware surfaces to minimize battery consumption.</string>

